    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** leading our projections at a 69.33 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Abbott (xERA 4.89) combined with a high-leverage leadoff spot makes him our most potent asset, even accounting for the platoon disadvantage. Similarly, **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (61.40) offer the strongest value, with **Casey Schmitt** benefiting from an 11% boost via his dynamic platoon edge against Lorenzen, and **Kazuma Okamoto** thriving against M\u00e1rquez, whose 5.58 xERA provides the most exploitable environment on our entire board. While **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** face a daunting task against Skubal, their base profiles remain too high to fade, even with the suppressed efficiency caused by the SP\u2019s elite skill.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge**, who finished just shy of the starting lineup with a 43.14 score. While he outperformed several starters, he ultimately fell victim to a -9% penalty due to a platoon disadvantage against Tolle, pushing him below the threshold required to crack our utility or outfield slots. Conversely, we are intentionally avoiding **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, and **Lars Nootbaar**, all of whom plummeted below our 40.0 floor due to a combination of elite opposing pitch framing and poor platoon splits. We remain particularly cautious regarding **Christian Yelich**, who, despite an encouraging 54.28 score, faces the formidable Skenes; while he retains a spot due to his high-volume leadoff role, his reliance on a dynamic platoon edge is the only thing keeping him above the marginal tier today. Owners should monitor weather updates, as the wind profile is currently suppressing **Lars Nootbaar**'s ceiling to the point of unplayability.",
